  "hindi": "तुझ सहयोगी के साथ इन्द्र ने सूर्य के चक्र को बल से तुरन्त नीचे दबाया, हे बिन्दु। विशाल शिखर पर घूमते हुए को; महान् द्रोह से दूर कर दिया गया सर्वायु।",
  "english": "With you as yoke-mate Indra pressed down the wheel of the sun by force, at once, O drop, rolling over the great ridge. From great malice the all-living was set away.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The second line is unclear: viśvāyu is taken as the nominative subject of dhāyi (apa dhāyi, 'was put away'), but what it refers to is not clear; vartamānam is read with cakram. snunā as an instrumental after adhi is unusual and the sense 'over the ridge' is tentative.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
