  "hindi": "इन्द्र ने मारा, अग्नि ने जलाया, हे बिन्दु, दस्युओं को दोपहर से पहले, मुठभेड़ में। गढ़ में, घर में, संकल्प से, जाने वालों के समान, बहुत हज़ार विनाशकों को उसने नीचे कुचल दिया।",
  "english": "Indra slew, Agni burned, O drop, the Dasyus before midday, in the encounter. In the stronghold, in the house, by resolve, as of the goers, he crushed down many thousands of destroyers.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Line 2: kratvā na yātām and śarvā are not understood. na is read 'like', yātām as a genitive plural 'of the goers', and śarvā as 'destroyers' (n. acc. pl.); other readings (e.g. śarvā as an instrumental 'by the weapon') are possible. Translation is literal only. purā with the ablative madhyaṃdināt: 'before midday'.",
