  "notes": "viśvasmāt sīm is read as an ablative of comparison ('than all'); sīm is a particle. dāsīḥ is taken as an adjective 'Dāsa'. The two addressees of line 2 (dual) are not named in the verse (the hymn's other verses suggest Indra and Soma). ni is read with amṛṇatam.",
